/P 73 0 R
/RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:9.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#FF0000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">Excess-3 Code :&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">  010110100100&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">1. Group bits in set                         of 4 in the given sequence.&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">2. Subtract 3 from each group.&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">3. Write back the BCD equivalent of each group.&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">Therefore,&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">0101  1010  0100&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">  5        10       4&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica"> -3        -3       -3&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">  2         7        1&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">Hence the decimal equivalent of given excess-3 code is 271.</span></p></body>)
